7	**Decided: walk chooses the declaration on the domains it compares today, the join instantiation, until rung W compares declared domains; it then re-instantiates the chosen generic by the promotion from the arguments' run-time types and converts at binding. It does not instantiate without conversion.**
8	- Why promote from run-time types. Walk has no static types, so "the checker's answer" is unknowable to it. Instantiating at the join without conversion, the later model's run-time instantiation (`Papers/Welterweight/dispatch.tick:187-193`), would give up answer 8 under walk everywhere, including the silent 32-bit arithmetic on a `ZZ64` variable that answer 8 ends (POSITIONS 2026-09-26, answer 8, its last sentence). For a program whose static types are concrete, as microGPT's are, the two paths then agree on arm and instance.
9	- Where they differ. A variable declared wider than its value (`same(n, w)`: compiled `[ZZ32, ZZ64]`, walk `[ZZ64, ZZ64]`, `O2Lone`; `O2Wide`), and an argument typed `Any` (`O2Lone`, `op(a, aw)`). The same body, a narrower instance; in the number tower every conversion goes between concrete types below `Number`, so the value stays inside the declared type (by reading, the ways note, way 4's soundness paragraph). A ledger row, opened at batch N's gather; not a stop.
10	- Between N and 7b. Rung K's choice stays on today's instantiation in `bestMatchInternal`'s subtyping pass, its code unchanged, and the winner is re-instantiated by the promotion before application: the one edit to `bestMatchInternal` that K's brief reserves (`CLIMB-BATCH-N.md`, rung K, "Files it may touch") is permitted for exactly this and reported. The coercion pass keeps generics as briefed, for the calls no declaration takes unconverted (`ProjectFortress/src/com/sun/fortress/interpreter/evaluator/values/OverloadedFunction.java:826`, opened and read). Re-dispatch of the converted call, `O2Z64`'s shape, cannot arise under walk before rung W lifts the load check that refuses the set today (`OverloadedFunction.java:527`; `captures/O2Z64.walk-*.txt`), so it is W's, as `option-2-soundness.md` section 4 lists.
