17	- Where walk converts: an instantiated function's arguments are converted at binding already, rung C's `Coercions.coerce` in `NonPrimitive.buildEnvFromParams` (`evaluator/values/NonPrimitive.java:212-257`, `:257`) and `typecheckParams` (`:134-185`, `:172`), reached from `FunctionClosure.applyInnerPossiblyGeneric` (`evaluator/values/FunctionClosure.java:176`, `:198`). So walk has the admission half; what refuses is the inference half: `scale(b, z)` instantiates `T = Number`, and the binding then refuses `Box[\RR64\]` for `Box[\Number\]` (FACTS, "An inferred generic refuses a coercion ...", `numerics-plan-fable/probes/one-shape/walk/ScaleZ.walk.txt`).
